\\"Classic illustration of the Cowardly Lion from L. Frank Baum's Wizard of Oz\\\" width=\\\"640\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" loading=\\\"eager\\\">\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</header>\\n\\n<main>\\n<section id=\\\"books\\\" class=\\\"wrap HDLmClass42bc71f1\\\">\\n  <h2>The 14 Oz Novels &mdash; Read in Order</h2>\\n  <p class=\\\"section-note\\\">Tap any title to open the complete book. Start with book&nbsp;1 or jump straight to a favourite.</p>\\n  <ul class=\\\"grid\\\">\\n    <li class=\\\"card featured\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 1 &middot; Start here</span><span class=\\\"title HDLmClass341bb96c\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1900</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/02.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 2</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1904</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/03.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 3</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Ozma of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1907</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/04.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 4</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1908</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/05.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 5</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Road to Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1909</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/06.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 6</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Emerald City of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1910</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/07.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 7</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Patchwork Girl of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1913</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/09.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 8</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Tik-Tok of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1914</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/10.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 9</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Scarecrow of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1915</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/11.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 10</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Rinkitink in Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1916</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/12.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 11</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Lost Princess of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1917</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/13.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 12</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Tin Woodman of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1918</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/14.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 13</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Magic of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1919</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/15.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 14</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Glinda of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1920</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n  </ul>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"wrap extras HDLmClass42bc71f1\\\">\\n  <h2>Also Worth Reading</h2>\\n  <p class=\\\"section-note\\\">Two Oz rarities most readers never find.</p>\\n  <ul class=\\\"grid\\\">\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/08.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Short stories</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Little Wizard Stories of Oz</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1913</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Read now &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n    <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/OzPlay.pdf\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Stage play &middot; PDF</span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Wizard of Oz: A Dramatic Composition</span><span class=\\\"year\\\">1902</span><span class=\\\"read\\\">Open PDF &rarr;</span></a></li>\\n  </ul>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"wrap HDLmClass6bfb2802\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"signup\\\">\\n    <h2>Get the Oz reading guide</h2>\\n    <p>One short email with the recommended reading order, character map and new additions to the library. No spam, unsubscribe any time.</p>\\n    <form action=\\\"#\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" novalidate>\\n      <label for=\\\"email\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px\\\">Email address</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" placeholder=\\\"you@example.com\\\" required>\\n      <button type=\\\"submit\\\">Send me the guide</button>\\n    </form>\\n    <small>Free forever. We never share your address.</small>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"wrap about HDLmClassde26d075\\\">\\n  <h2>About this library</h2>\\n  <p>Between 1900 and 1920 L. Frank Baum wrote fourteen full-length Oz novels, beginning with <em>The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</em> and ending with <em>Glinda of Oz</em>. Every one of them is in the public domain, and every one is collected here as clean, readable text &mdash; no paywall, no account, nothing to install.</p>\\n  <p>New to Oz? Read the books in order, starting with <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">book&nbsp;1</a>. Already know Dorothy&rsquo;s story? Many readers say <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/02.htm\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</a> and <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/07.htm\\\">The Patchwork Girl of Oz</a> are the most inventive of the series.</p>\\n</section>\\n</main>\\n\\n<footer class=\\\"wrap HDLmClassde26d075\\\">\\n  <p>The Wizard of Oz books by L. Frank Baum &mdash; free full texts, public domain. <a href=\\\"#books\\\">Browse all books</a></p>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"sticky HDLmClass5f47a094\\\">\\n  <a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start Reading Book&nbsp;1 &mdash; Free</a>\\n</div>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Fixed typo Wixard\",\"Why\":\"Trust and SEO\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass341bb96c\"},{\"What\":\"Added CTA\",\"Why\":\"Drives clicks\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassde26d075\"},{\"What\":\"Card grid\",\"Why\":\"More clicks\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass42bc71f1\"},{\"What\":\"Email signup\",\"Why\":\"Builds list\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass6bfb2802\"},{\"What\":\"SEO meta tags\",\"Why\":\"More traffic\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClasse3563e74\"},{\"What\":\"Mobile styles\",\"Why\":\"Less bounce\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass5f47a094\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm planning a full overhaul of the plain link list page—adding proper structure, a hero section, headings, SEO meta tags, CTA cards, reading progress, newsletter signup, fixing the \"Wixard\" typo to \"Wizard\", and responsive design. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes over the concatenated What+Why text for each improvement, which will take careful manual calculation.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash...\n\nContinuing the hash computation, I keep multiplying by 33, taking mod 2^32, and adding each character's ASCII value in sequence through 'y', 'p', and 'o'.\n\nStill computing the hash step by step...\n\nStill computing the hash values...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for O(79): 3670706557*33 minus 28*4294967296 gives diff 874,232,093, plus 79 equals 874,232,172. Now converting this final value to hex.\n\nWorking through the hex conversion digit by digit, I get 341bb96c, giving hash1 = HDLmClass341bb96c. This manual arithmetic is proving extremely tedious.\n\nNow I'm computing a djb2-style hash for a second string, \"Added CTADrives clicks,\" manually multiplying and adding ASCII values step by step through each character.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through characters T, A, D...\n\nr, i, v, e...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for i, c, k, working through each character's multiplication and modular reduction step by step.\n\nFinishing the hex conversion gives de26d075, so hash2 becomes \"HDLmClassde26d075\". This manual computation is taking a while, so I'll limit myself to about 5-6 improvements total to keep things manageable, trying to keep the description strings short for each one.\n\nFor improvement 3, I'm testing \"Card grid\" paired with \"More clicks\" as a shorter string and working through its hash computation step by step.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining characters...\n\nContinuing the division through the remaining digits, I get hex 42bc71f1 as the final result.\n\nNow I'm computing the DJB2 hash for the fourth improvement idea, \"Email signup\" with \"Builds list,\" running through each character's multiplication and addition steps.\n\nStill computing the hash value...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for characters 'd', 's', and space...\n\n', then 'l', 'i', 's', 't', and now converting the final running hash value to hexadecimal.\n\nContinuing division into hex digits gives 6bfb2802, so Hash4 becomes \"HDLmClass6bfb2802\". Now moving on to Improvement 5, concatenating \"SEO meta tags\" and \"More traffic\" into a string to hash next.\n\nStill computing the hash digits...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through steps 13-15, working through modular arithmetic for characters s, M, o...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through each character...\n\nContinuing the hash computation: f(105) gives 2,978,889,713, then c(99) yields 3,814,080,116, and now I'm converting that final value to hexadecimal by dividing through successive powers of 16 to extract each digit.\n\nI get e3563e74 as the final hex hash, giving Hash5 = \"HDLmClasse3563e74\". Now I'm moving to a sixth improvement idea — \"Mobile styles\" with reasoning \"Less bounce\" — and starting the djb2 hash computation on the combined string \"Mobile stylesLess bounce\" by processing each character's ASCII value through the multiply-by-33-plus-char formula.\n\nStill computing the hash values...\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nContinuing the division gives hex digits 4, 7, a, 0, 9, 4, so the final hash is 5f47a094, giving Hash6 = HDLmClass5f47a094. That's six improvements done, so now I'll move on to building the next piece.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm planning a full overhaul of the plain link list page—adding proper structure, a hero section, headings, SEO meta tags, CTA cards, reading progress, newsletter signup, fixing the \"Wixard\" typo to \"Wizard\", and responsive design. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes over the concatenated What+Why text for each improvement, which will take careful manual calculation.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash...\n\nContinuing the hash computation, I keep multiplying by 33, taking mod 2^32, and adding each character's ASCII value in sequence through 'y', 'p', and 'o'.\n\nStill computing the hash step by step...\n\nStill computing the hash values...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for O(79): 3670706557*33 minus 28*4294967296 gives diff 874,232,093, plus 79 equals 874,232,172. Now converting this final value to hex.\n\nWorking through the hex conversion digit by digit, I get 341bb96c, giving hash1 = HDLmClass341bb96c. This manual arithmetic is proving extremely tedious.\n\nNow I'm computing a djb2-style hash for a second string, \"Added CTADrives clicks,\" manually multiplying and adding ASCII values step by step through each character.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through characters T, A, D...\n\nr, i, v, e...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for i, c, k, working through each character's multiplication and modular reduction step by step.\n\nFinishing the hex conversion gives de26d075, so hash2 becomes \"HDLmClassde26d075\". This manual computation is taking a while, so I'll limit myself to about 5-6 improvements total to keep things manageable, trying to keep the description strings short for each one.\n\nFor improvement 3, I'm testing \"Card grid\" paired with \"More clicks\" as a shorter string and working through its hash computation step by step.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining characters...\n\nContinuing the division through the remaining digits, I get hex 42bc71f1 as the final result.\n\nNow I'm computing the DJB2 hash for the fourth improvement idea, \"Email signup\" with \"Builds list,\" running through each character's multiplication and addition steps.\n\nStill computing the hash value...\n\nContinuing the hash computation for characters 'd', 's', and space...\n\n', then 'l', 'i', 's', 't', and now converting the final running hash value to hexadecimal.\n\nContinuing division into hex digits gives 6bfb2802, so Hash4 becomes \"HDLmClass6bfb2802\". Now moving on to Improvement 5, concatenating \"SEO meta tags\" and \"More traffic\" into a string to hash next.\n\nStill computing the hash digits...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through steps 13-15, working through modular arithmetic for characters s, M, o...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through each character...\n\nContinuing the hash computation: f(105) gives 2,978,889,713, then c(99) yields 3,814,080,116, and now I'm converting that final value to hexadecimal by dividing through successive powers of 16 to extract each digit.\n\nI get e3563e74 as the final hex hash, giving Hash5 = \"HDLmClasse3563e74\". Now I'm moving to a sixth improvement idea — \"Mobile styles\" with reasoning \"Less bounce\" — and starting the djb2 hash computation on the combined string \"Mobile stylesLess bounce\" by processing each character's ASCII value through the multiply-by-33-plus-char formula.\n\nStill computing the hash values...\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nContinuing the division gives hex digits 4, 7, a, 0, 9, 4, so the final hash is 5f47a094, giving Hash6 = HDLmClass5f47a094. That's six improvements done, so now I'll move on to building the next piece.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":4382,"completion_tokens":21161,"total_tokens":25543,"cost":0.550935,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.550935,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.02191,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.529025},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":14176,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0},"server_tool_use_details":{"web_search_requests":0}}}
