rdly Lion from The Wonderful Wizard of Oz\\\" width=\\\"640\\\" height=\\\"800\\\">\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</header>\\n\\n<section id=\\\"books\\\" class=\\\"HDLmClass5A1C085A\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <h2>The Oz series in reading order</h2>\\n    <p class=\\\"section-note\\\">Baum wrote 14 Oz novels, plus a stage adaptation and a book of short stories. Tap any title to begin reading instantly.</p>\\n    <ul class=\\\"grid\\\">\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 1</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title HDLmClass7C7EA3CB\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1900 &middot; where Dorothy&rsquo;s journey begins</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 2</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/02.htm\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1904 &middot; Tip, Jack Pumpkinhead and Mombi</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/02.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 3</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/03.htm\\\">Ozma of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1907 &middot; Dorothy returns with Billina</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/03.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 4</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/04.htm\\\">Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1908 &middot; underground adventures</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/04.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 5</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/05.htm\\\">The Road to Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1909 &middot; the Shaggy Man and Button-Bright</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/05.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 6</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/06.htm\\\">The Emerald City of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1910 &middot; the Nome King invades</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/06.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 7</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/07.htm\\\">The Patchwork Girl of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1913 &middot; Scraps and the Glass Cat</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/07.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 8</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/09.htm\\\">Tik-Tok of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1914 &middot; the clockwork man&rsquo;s quest</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/09.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 9</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/10.htm\\\">The Scarecrow of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1915 &middot; Baum&rsquo;s own favorite</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/10.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 10</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/11.htm\\\">Rinkitink in Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1916 &middot; Prince Inga and the pearls</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/11.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 11</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/12.htm\\\">The Lost Princess of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1917 &middot; Ozma disappears</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/12.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 12</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/13.htm\\\">The Tin Woodman of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1918 &middot; Nick Chopper&rsquo;s lost love</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/13.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 13</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/14.htm\\\">The Magic of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1919 &middot; the word of transformation</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/14.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Book 14</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/15.htm\\\">Glinda of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1920 &middot; the final Baum Oz novel</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/15.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card bonus\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Bonus &middot; Short stories</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/08.htm\\\">Little Wizard Stories of Oz</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1913 &middot; six short tales for younger readers</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/08.htm\\\">Read now &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card bonus\\\">\\n        <div class=\\\"num\\\">Bonus &middot; Stage script (PDF)</div>\\n        <div class=\\\"title\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/OzPlay.pdf\\\">The Wizard of Oz: A Dramatic Composition</a></div>\\n        <div class=\\\"year\\\">1902 &middot; the original musical extravaganza</div>\\n        <a class=\\\"read\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/OzPlay.pdf\\\">Open PDF &rarr;</a>\\n      </li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"HDLmClassBB6B5EF3\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"signup\\\">\\n      <h2>Get a reading list &amp; a new Oz chapter each week</h2>\\n      <p>Enter your email and we&rsquo;ll send you the recommended Oz reading order plus one hand-picked chapter every week &mdash; so you actually finish the series.</p>\\n      <form action=\\\"#\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" onsubmit=\\\"var e=document.getElementById('oz-email');if(!e.value){return false;}document.getElementById('oz-thanks').style.display='block';return false;\\\">\\n        <label for=\\\"oz-email\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px\\\">Email address</label>\\n        <input id=\\\"oz-email\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" placeholder=\\\"you@example.com\\\" required>\\n        <button class=\\\"btn btn-gold\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Send me the reading list</button>\\n      </form>\\n      <div id=\\\"oz-thanks\\\" style=\\\"display:none;margin-top:12px;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#fff\\\">Thank you! Check your inbox for the Oz reading order.</div>\\n      <small>One email a week. Unsubscribe any time. We never share your address.</small>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<section class=\\\"faq HDLmClassC722F624\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <h2>Questions readers ask</h2>\\n    <details>\\n      <summary>Are these books really free?</summary>\\n      <p>Yes. L. Frank Baum&rsquo;s Oz novels are in the public domain in the United States, so you can read every title on this site at no cost and with no account.</p>\\n    </details>\\n    <details>\\n      <summary>Which Oz book should I read first?</summary>\\n      <p>Start with <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz (1900)</a>, then follow the numbered order above. Each later book stands alone reasonably well, but characters carry over.</p>\\n    </details>\\n    <details>\\n      <summary>Can I read on my phone?</summary>\\n      <p>Yes &mdash; the text reflows for phones and tablets, so you can pick up any chapter anywhere.</p>\\n    </details>\\n    <details>\\n      <summary>Is the movie the same as the book?</summary>\\n      <p>No. The 1939 film adapts only the first novel, and changes many details. The books continue for thirteen more adventures beyond the movie&rsquo;s ending.</p>\\n    </details>\\n    <div class=\\\"cta-row\\\" style=\\\"margin-top:18px\\\">\\n      <a class=\\\"btn\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Begin reading The Wonderful Wizard of Oz &rarr;</a>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</section>\\n\\n<footer class=\\\"HDLmClassC722F624\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <p>The Marvelous Land of Oz &mdash; the complete Oz series by L. Frank Baum, free to read online. Public domain texts.</p>\\n    <p><a href=\\\"#books\\\">All books</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start reading</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/OzPlay.pdf\\\">1902 stage script (PDF)</a></p>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"sticky HDLmClassC722F624\\\">\\n  <span>All 14 Oz books &mdash; free</span>\\n  <a class=\\\"btn btn-gold\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start Book 1</a>\\n</div>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Fixed 'Wixard' typo\",\"Why\":\"Typos cut trust\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass7C7EA3CB\"},{\"What\":\"Added hero CTA\",\"Why\":\"Guides readers\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassC722F624\"},{\"What\":\"Email signup\",\"Why\":\"Captures leads\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassBB6B5EF3\"},{\"What\":\"Book card grid\",\"Why\":\"Easier scanning\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass5A1C085A\"},{\"What\":\"SEO meta tags\",\"Why\":\"More traffic\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassE3563E74\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"Since I only have a markdown-style extraction rather than the actual HTML, I'll need to build a full improved page from scratch—preserving all links and images while fixing the \"Wixard\"→\"Wizard\" typo, adding a hero section, CTA, email signup, structured book cards, SEO meta tags, and mobile responsiveness. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes for each improvement's What+Why text, which I'll have to do by hand.\n\nI'm weighing how to keep this manageable: doing 500+ multiplication operations across many improvements is too error-prone, so I should limit myself to fewer improvements with shorter, still-meaningful What/Why strings, and work through the hash calculations carefully one character at a time.\n\nI'll shorten the strings to keep the hashing manageable, planning around six improvements with concise \"what/why\" pairs like fixing a typo for trust, adding a hero and CTA, an email signup, a book grid, and SEO tags, each trimmed to roughly 30-40 characters combined.\n\nGiven the effort involved in manually hashing each string character by character, I'm reconsidering whether to trim down to five improvements to reduce the total computation needed, then starting the character-by-character conversion for the first string.\n\nContinuing the hash computation for e and d, applying modulo 2^32 wraparound once the accumulated value exceeds the 32-bit range.\n\nContinuing the hash computation for characters W and i, verifying each multiplication and modular reduction step by step.\n\nContinuing the modular reduction chain, I compute steps 11 through 13, tracking each multiply-and-mod operation for the successive letters, arriving at a difference of 3 after processing 'd'.\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation, I process the space character (32) next, getting a difference of 1,696,339,538, then move to the 't' character (116), multiplying by 33 and adding 116 to continue the rolling hash calculation.\n\nContinuing the modular exponentiation calculation, I get 658,808,030 for step 19, then move into step 20 computing 658,808,030*33 + 84.\n\nContinuing the hash computation for characters 23-25, applying multiply-by-33 and modular reduction steps for \"o\", \"s\", and space, tracking each running hash value with verification checks.\n\nContinuing the modular reduction for characters 27 and 28, computing 907,632,320*33+117 and 4,182,062,901*33+116 modulo their respective bases, verifying each multiplication with the split-sum check.\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation, working through each character's contribution step by step...\n\nNow converting the running difference value to hexadecimal.\n\nI'm working through the digit-by-digit hex conversion, getting 7C7EA3CB, and now double-checking that value.\n\nSum checks out: 2,088,674,251, so Hash1 = HDLmClass7C7EA3CB. That took 34 steps, so I'll speed things up by choosing shorter strings for the remaining improvements.\n\nFor improvement 2, I'm computing the hash for \"Added hero CTAGuides readers\" by running the djb2-style multiply-and-add over each character. Still working through the hash iterations...\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation through the next several characters, tracking each multiply-by-33 step and reducing mod 2^32 as I go.\n\nContinuing the hash computation...\n\nContinuing through the modular reduction for characters i, d, e, working through each multiplication and subtraction step to get the running hash value.\n\nContinuing the hash computation, I process characters 23-25 (e, a, d), each time multiplying by 33 and reducing modulo the appropriate power of 2, tracking the running difference through each step.\n\nContinuing the hex conversion digit by digit, I arrive at 0xC722F624 and start double-checking this value against my earlier calculation.\n\nContinuing the djb2 hash computation character by character through the string, applying the multiply-by-33-plus-char-code and overflow wraparound at each step.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through characters i, g, n, applying the multiply-by-33 and modulo reduction steps to get the running value down to 8,589,934,592.\n\nContinuing the modular hash computation through the next several characters...\n\nContinuing the hash computation...\n\n27) letter=115: 876,187,264*33 computes to 3,144,376,051, and now I'm converting that value to hexadecimal, working through it byte by byte to find its representation.\n\nI finish computing the hex digits and confirm the hash equals HDLmClassBB6B5EF3, verifying by reconstructing the number from its hex components. I then move to the next improvement item, combining its \"what\" and \"why\" text into a string for the fourth hash: \"Book card gridEasier scanning\".\n\nNow I'm running the DJB2-style hash algorithm on this string, multiplying the running hash by 33 and adding each character code, wrapping with modulo 2^32 at each step where it overflows.\n\nStill computing the hash values...\n\nContinuing the hash computation... rolling through characters g, r, i, d with modular multiplication and reduction at each step, tracking the running value through steps 12-14.\n\nContinuing the hash computation...\n\nStill computing the hash rounds...\n\nContinuing the modulo computation for step 29, then converting the result 1,511,786,586 into hexadecimal digit by digit.\n\nI verify by reconstructing the hex value back into decimal, confirming it matches: 1,511,786,586. So the fourth hash comes out to HDLmClass5A1C085A.\n\nNow moving to improvement 5, combining \"SEO meta tags\" with \"More traffic\" into a single string and running it character by character through the DJB2-style hash computation, updating the running hash value with each multiply-and-add step.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through characters t, a, and space...\n\nContinuing the rolling hash computation...\n\nStill computing the rolling hash values...\n\ncompletes to 3,814,080,116, then I'm converting that value to hexadecimal by successively dividing out powers of 16, building up the digits E3563E...\n\nfinally getting E3563E74. So Hash5 comes out to HDLmClassE3563E74.\n\nNow I'll build the polished landing page, preserving all 16 original links, adding a hero, CTAs, a reading order grid, an email capture, and a footer, avoiding any invented external commerce links. I'm writing the HTML with inline responsive CSS and marking the changed sections with the hash class.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Since I only have a markdown-style extraction rather than the actual HTML, I'll need to build a full improved page from scratch—preserving all links and images while fixing the \"Wixard\"→\"Wizard\" typo, adding a hero section, CTA, email signup, structured book cards, SEO meta tags, and mobile responsiveness. I also need to compute DJB2 hashes for each improvement's What+Why text, which I'll have to do by hand.\n\nI'm weighing how to keep this manageable: doing 500+ multiplication operations across many improvements is too error-prone, so I should limit myself to fewer improvements with shorter, still-meaningful What/Why strings, and work through the hash calculations carefully one character at a time.\n