ing:18px}.shop .item h3{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:1.05rem}.shop .item p{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:.95rem;color:var(--muted)}.faq details{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e9e0cb;border-radius:10px;padding:12px 16px;margin-bottom:10px}.faq summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:700}footer.site{border-top:1px solid #e6ddc7;background:#fffdf7;padding:26px 0 96px;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}.stickybar{position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;background:#fffdf7;border-top:1px solid #e6ddc7;padding:10px 16px;display:none;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:12px;z-index:30;box-shadow:0 -6px 18px rgba(0,0,0,.08)}.stickybar span{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,sans-serif;font-size:.9rem;font-weight:600}@media(max-width:860px){.hero,.signup{grid-template-columns:1fr}.hero h1{font-size:2rem}figure.heroimg{order:-1}.stickybar{display:flex}header.site .nav-cta{display:none}}</style></head><body><header class=\\\"site HDLmClass708141fc\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><a class=\\\"brand\\\" href=\\\"/\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</a><a class=\\\"nav-cta\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start Reading Free &rarr;</a></div></header><main><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><section class=\\\"hero HDLmClass708141fc\\\"><div><h1>Read All 14 Wizard of Oz Books &mdash; Free Online</h1><p class=\\\"sub\\\">Every Oz novel by L. Frank Baum, from <em>The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</em> (1900) to <em>Glinda of Oz</em> (1920) &mdash; plus bonus stories and the original 1902 stage play. No signup, no paywall, no apps.</p><div class=\\\"btns\\\"><a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start Book 1 Now</a><a class=\\\"btn btn-secondary\\\" href=\\\"#library\\\">Browse All Books</a></div><ul class=\\\"trust\\\"><li>100% free to read</li><li>Public domain texts</li><li>Works on phone, tablet &amp; desktop</li><li>16 titles, 1900&ndash;1920</li></ul></div><figure class=\\\"heroimg\\\"><img src=\\\"https://themarvelouslandof.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/Wizard+of+Oz+-+The+Lion.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Classic illustration of the Cowardly Lion from L. Frank Baum's The Wonderful Wizard of Oz\\\" width=\\\"900\\\" height=\\\"1200\\\" loading=\\\"eager\\\"><figcaption>W. W. Denslow&rsquo;s original illustration of the Cowardly Lion (1900).</figcaption></figure></section><section id=\\\"library\\\" class=\\\"HDLmClassc3229499\\\"><h2>The Complete Oz Library</h2><p class=\\\"section-sub\\\">Click any title to begin reading instantly &mdash; the 14 Oz novels in publication order, with two bonus titles.</p><ul class=\\\"grid\\\"><li><a class=\\\"card start\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"tag\\\">Start here</span><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 1</span><span class=\\\"t HDLmClass33b8f5b5\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1900 &middot; Dorothy meets the Scarecrow, Tin Woodman &amp; Lion</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/02.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 2</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1904</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/03.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 3</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">Ozma of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1907</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/04.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 4</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1908</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/05.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 5</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Road to Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1909</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/06.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 6</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Emerald City of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1910</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/07.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 7</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Patchwork Girl of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1913</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/09.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 8</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">Tik-Tok of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1914</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/10.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 9</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Scarecrow of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1915</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/11.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 10</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">Rinkitink in Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1916</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/12.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 11</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Lost Princess of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1917</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/13.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 12</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Tin Woodman of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1918</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/14.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 13</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Magic of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1919</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/15.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">Book 14</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">Glinda of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1920</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/08.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"tag\\\">Bonus</span><span class=\\\"num\\\">Short stories</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">Little Wizard Stories of Oz</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1913 &middot; six short tales</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Read free &rarr;</span></a></li><li><a class=\\\"card\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/OzPlay.pdf\\\"><span class=\\\"tag\\\">PDF</span><span class=\\\"num\\\">Stage play</span><span class=\\\"t\\\">The Wizard of Oz: A Dramatic Composition</span><span class=\\\"y\\\">1902 &middot; opens as a PDF</span><span class=\\\"go\\\">Open PDF &rarr;</span></a></li></ul></section><section class=\\\"HDLmClassdb7c1453\\\"><div class=\\\"panel signup\\\"><div><h2>Get a new Oz chapter in your inbox</h2><p class=\\\"section-sub\\\">Join free readers getting one classic Oz chapter a week, plus reading guides for parents and teachers.</p><form class=\\\"sub\\\" action=\\\"/subscribe\\\" method=\\\"post\\\"><label for=\\\"email\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px\\\">Email address</label><input id=\\\"email\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" placeholder=\\\"you@example.com\\\" required autocomplete=\\\"email\\\"><button class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Send Me Chapter 1</button></form><p class=\\\"fineprint\\\">One email a week. Unsubscribe anytime. We never share your address.</p></div><div><h3 style=\\\"margin-top:0\\\">Prefer to just start reading?</h3><p class=\\\"section-sub\\\">No email needed &mdash; the full text of every book is open right now.</p><a class=\\\"btn btn-secondary\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Open The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</a></div></div></section><section class=\\\"HDLmClass368dbc6d\\\"><h2>Love these books? Take Oz with you</h2><p class=\\\"section-sub\\\">Reading online is free forever. If you&rsquo;d like a keepsake edition or an audio version, these help support the site.</p><div class=\\\"shop\\\"><div class=\\\"item\\\"><h3>Illustrated print editions</h3><p>Hardcover and paperback sets with the original Denslow and Neill artwork.</p><a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=wizard+of+oz+l+frank+baum+illustrated\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow sponsored\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Shop Print Editions</a></div><div class=\\\"item\\\"><h3>Audiobooks</h3><p>Listen to the Oz series narrated end to end &mdash; great for road trips and bedtime.</p><a class=\\\"btn btn-secondary\\\" href=\\\"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=wizard+of+oz+audiobook+l+frank+baum\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow sponsored\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">Browse Audiobooks</a></div><div class=\\\"item\\\"><h3>Support this library</h3><p>Help keep all 16 Oz titles online, ad-light and free for every reader.</p><a class=\\\"btn btn-secondary\\\" href=\\\"#library\\\">Share the Library</a></div></div></section><section class=\\\"faq HDLmClasse3563e74\\\"><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><details open><summary>Are these Oz books really free?</summary><p>Yes. Every title here is in the public domain in the United States, so you can read the complete text online at no cost and without creating an account.</p></details><details><summary>Which Oz book should I read first?</summary><p>Start with <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</a> (1900), then follow the numbered order through <em>Glinda of Oz</em> (1920).</p></details><details><summary>Can I read on my phone?</summary><p>Yes &mdash; the library and every book page work in any mobile browser, with no app to install.</p></details><details><summary>How many Oz books did L. Frank Baum write?</summary><p>Baum wrote 14 Oz novels. This site also includes <em>Little Wizard Stories of Oz</em> (1913) and his 1902 stage adaptation.</p></details></section></div></main><footer class=\\\"site HDLmClassb43a950c\\\"><div class=\\\"wrap\\\"><p>The Marvelous Land of Oz &mdash; the complete Oz series by L. Frank Baum, free to read online. Texts are in the public domain. Product links may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.</p><p><a href=\\\"#library\\\">All books</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start reading</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/OzPlay.pdf\\\">1902 stage play (PDF)</a></p></div></footer><div class=\\\"stickybar HDLmClassb43a950c\\\"><span>Book 1, free &amp; instant</span><a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" style=\\\"padding:11px 16px\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start Reading</a></div></body></html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Hero with CTA\",\"Why\":\"Boosts reading starts\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass708141fc\"},{\"What\":\"Book cover grid\",\"Why\":\"Easier browsing\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassc3229499\"},{\"What\":\"Email signup\",\"Why\":\"Captures leads\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassdb7c1453\"},{\"What\":\"Shop CTA\",\"Why\":\"Adds revenue\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass368dbc6d\"},{\"What\":\"Responsive layout\",\"Why\":\"Cuts bounce\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassb43a950c\"},{\"What\":\"Fixed typo Wixard\",\"Why\":\"Builds trust\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass33b8f5b5\"},{\"What\":\"SEO meta tags\",\"Why\":\"More traffic\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClasse3563e74\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm redesigning the plain HTML page into a polished landing page with hero section, CTA, book cards, and email signup, then need to compute DJB2 hashes for each improvement's What+Why description to document the changes.\n\nGiven how error-prone manual hashing over long strings would be, I'm deciding to keep the improvement descriptions short and limit the count to around five items so the hash computations stay manageable.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash values...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through several more rounds of multiplication and modular reduction, working through h8 to h13.\n\nStill computing the hash chain values...\n\nWait, I caught an arithmetic slip earlier — h21 was computed wrong. Let me redo it: 4294967296*31 actually equals 133143986176, not what I had, so h21 should be 216885395, not 316885395. I need to redo the hash chain starting from h22 with this corrected value.\n\nContinuing hash computation...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through more characters, I get down to h34 landing on 1887519228, and now I'm converting that final value into hexadecimal by breaking it down through powers of two.\n\nThe result comes out to 0x708141FC, giving me the final hash string \"HDLmClass708141FC\" once I verify the arithmetic checks out.\n\nI'll go with lowercase hex to keep things simple, then move on to computing the hash for the next improvement string, \"Book cover gridEasier browsing\", by summing up each character's ASCII value.\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nStill computing the hash iterations...\n\nStill computing the hash iteration...\n\nThe sum checks out, confirming Hash2. Now I'm computing the DJB2 hash for the string \"Email signupCaptures leads\" character by character, tracking the running hash value through modular multiplication and overflow wraparound at each step.\n\nContinuing the rolling hash computation through the remaining characters of the string.\n\nContinuing the rolling hash computation through the remaining characters, then converting the final accumulated value into hexadecimal by successively dividing out place values.\n\nI get 0xDB7C1453, and after verifying the sum checks out, the hash comes to HDLmClassdb7c1453. Now I'm moving on to look at improvement 4 regarding audiobook and print links.\n\nFor revenue, I'm testing a shorter CTA phrase like \"Shop CTA\" / \"Adds revenue\" and computing its hash by walking through the character codes.\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nStill computing the hash step by step...\n\nContinuing the diff computation, I get 915258477, then convert it to hexadecimal digit by digit through repeated division, arriving at 0x368DBC6D, and now I'm double-checking the sum of the hex digit values.\n\nFor improvement 5, I settle on the phrasing \"Responsive layout\" / \"Cuts bounce\" and combine them into a 28-character string, then start summing ASCII values for each character.\n\nI continue running the hash computation through each character, applying the multiply-by-33 and add-character-code steps with modular wraparound at each stage.\n\nStill computing the hash iterations...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining characters, then converting the final accumulated value into hexadecimal by dividing out successive byte places.\n\nNow computing hash5 for \"Fixed typo WixardBuilds trust\" using the djb2 algorithm, processing each character's ASCII value through the hash multiplication step.\n\nStill computing the rolling hash step by step...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through more characters, tracking the running difference value as it grows.\n\nNow I'm converting the final accumulated number into hex by dividing repeatedly by powers of 16 and finding remainders.\n\nI verify the hex digits sum back to the correct decimal value, confirming the class hash is 0x33B8F5B5, then start considering an optional improvement around trust badges to reduce user hesitation.\n\nStill computing the hash check...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through characters \"r\", \"e\", \"sp\", \"t\", tracking the running difference at each step.\n\nAfter processing the final character, I convert the resulting number to hexadecimal by successive division, arriving at 0xE3563E74 as the hash value, and now I want to double-check this result.\n\nVerification confirms the sum matches: 3814080116, so the hash is HDLmClasse3563e74. Now I'm planning the HTML structure — proper doctype and SEO metadata, a hero section with a headline and primary CTA, a grid showcasing all 14 novels plus extras with year and badge info, a buy CTA linking to an Amazon search, and an email signup form.\n\nI still need to add a footer with a public domain note, keep the CSS inline and responsive, fix the \"Wixard\" typo to \"Wonderful Wizard of Oz\", and make sure every new or changed element gets a hashed class name. I'll write the whole HTML as a single line to avoid escaping issues with newlines in the JSON string.\n\nWriting the HTML document...\n\nListing out the remaining book entries...","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm redesigning the plain HTML page into a polished landing page with hero section, CTA, book cards, and email signup, then need to compute DJB2 hashes for each improvement's What+Why description to document the changes.\n\nGiven how error-prone manual hashing over long strings would be, I'm deciding to keep the improvement descriptions short and limit the count to around five items so the hash computations stay manageable.\n\nComputing DJB2 hash values...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through several more rounds of multiplication and modular reduction, working through h8 to h13.\n\nStill computing the hash chain values...\n\nWait, I caught an arithmetic slip earlier — h21 was computed wrong. Let me redo it: 4294967296*31 actually equals 133143986176, not what I had, so h21 should be 216885395, not 316885395. I need to redo the hash chain starting from h22 with this corrected value.\n\nContinuing hash computation...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through more characters, I get down to h34 landing on 1887519228, and now I'm converting that final value into hexadecimal by breaking it down through powers of two.\n\nThe result comes out to 0x708141FC, giving me the final hash string \"HDLmClass708141FC\" once I verify the arithmetic checks out.\n\nI'll go with lowercase hex to keep things simple, then move on to computing the hash for the next improvement string, \"Book cover gridEasier browsing\", by summing up each character's ASCII value.\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nStill computing the hash iterations...\n\nStill computing the hash iteration...\n\nThe sum checks out, confirming Hash2. Now I'm computing the DJB2 hash for the string \"Email signupCaptures leads\" character by character, tracking the running hash value through modular multiplication and overflow wraparound at each step.\n\nContinuing the rolling hash computation through the remaining characters of the string.\n\nContinuing the rolling hash computation through the remaining characters, then converting the final accumulated value into hexadecimal by successively dividing out place values.\n\nI get 0xDB7C1453, and after verifying the sum checks out, the hash comes to HDLmClassdb7c1453. Now I'm moving on to look at improvement 4 regarding audiobook and print links.\n\nFor revenue, I'm testing a shorter CTA phrase like \"Shop CTA\" / \"Adds revenue\" and computing its hash by walking through the character codes.\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nStill computing the hash step by step...\n\nContinuing the diff computation, I get 915258477, then convert it to hexadecimal digit by digit through repeated division, arriving at 0x368DBC6D, and now I'm double-checking the sum of the hex digit values.\n\nFor improvement 5, I settle on the phrasing \"Responsive layout\" / \"Cuts bounce\" and combine them into a 28-character string, then start summing ASCII values for each character.\n\nI continue running the hash computation through each character, applying the multiply-by-33 and add-character-code steps with modular wraparound at each stage.\n\nStill computing the hash iterations...\n\nContinuing the hash computation through the remaining characters, then converting the final accumulated value into hexadecimal by dividing out successive byte places.\n\nNow computing hash5 for \"Fixed typo