rd.featured{border:2px solid var(--gold);background:#fffdf5;}\\n.badge{display:inline-block;background:var(--gold);color:#26200a;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,\\\"Segoe UI\\\",Arial,sans-serif;font-size:.68rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;border-radius:4px;padding:2px 7px;margin-top:6px;}\\n.signup{background:#0f7b5f;color:#fff;border-radius:12px;padding:26px 22px;margin:10px 0 0;}\\n.signup h2{color:#fff;}\\n.signup p{color:#e3f2ec;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,\\\"Segoe UI\\\",Arial,sans-serif;font-size:.95rem;margin:0 0 16px;}\\n.signup form{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;}\\n.signup input[type=email]{flex:1 1 240px;padding:13px 14px;border:1px solid #b9d9cd;border-radius:8px;font-size:1rem;font-family:inherit;}\\n.signup .fineprint{font-size:.78rem;color:#cfe8de;margin:12px 0 0;}\\nfooter{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:22px;padding:22px 0 40px;font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,\\\"Segoe UI\\\",Arial,sans-serif;font-size:.85rem;color:#63705f;}\\nfooter a{color:var(--emerald-dark);}\\n.sticky{position:sticky;bottom:0;background:#083f31;padding:10px 14px;display:none;justify-content:center;box-shadow:0 -4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.25);z-index:20;}\\n@media (max-width:640px){.hero{padding:24px 0;}.hero-art{order:-1;max-width:230px;}.btn{width:100%;text-align:center;}.sticky{display:flex;}.sticky .btn{padding:12px 18px;}}\\n</style>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n\\n<header class=\\\"hero HDLmClass47d5c5b\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"hero-copy\\\">\\n      <p class=\\\"kicker\\\">Free &middot; Complete &middot; No signup needed</p>\\n      <h1>All 14 Wizard of Oz books by L. Frank Baum &mdash; free to read online</h1>\\n      <p class=\\\"lede\\\">The complete original Oz series, in publication order, plus the 1902 stage play and the Little Wizard Stories. Start reading in seconds on any device.</p>\\n      <div class=\\\"cta-row HDLmClass89ba1bed\\\">\\n        <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start reading Book 1 &rarr;</a>\\n        <a class=\\\"btn btn-secondary\\\" href=\\\"#books\\\">See all 14 books</a>\\n      </div>\\n      <p class=\\\"trust\\\">Public-domain texts &middot; No ads to click through &middot; Works on phone, tablet and desktop</p>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"hero-art\\\">\\n      <img src=\\\"https://themarvelouslandof.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/Wizard+of+Oz+-+The+Lion.jpg\\\" alt=\\\"Classic illustration of the Cowardly Lion from The Wonderful Wizard of Oz\\\" width=\\\"600\\\" height=\\\"800\\\" loading=\\\"eager\\\">\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</header>\\n\\n<main class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n\\n  <section id=\\\"books\\\">\\n    <h2>The complete Oz library</h2>\\n    <p class=\\\"section-note HDLmClass80a70a99\\\">New to Oz? Read them in this order &mdash; each title opens the full text.</p>\\n    <ul class=\\\"grid HDLmClass80a70a99\\\">\\n      <li class=\\\"card featured\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">1</span><span><span class=\\\"title HDLmClass6564b1f4\\\">The Wonderful Wizard of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1900 &middot; Full text</span><span class=\\\"badge\\\">Start here</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/02.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">2</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Marvelous Land of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1904 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/03.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">3</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Ozma of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1907 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/04.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">4</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Dorothy and the Wizard in Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1908 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/05.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">5</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Road to Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1909 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/06.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">6</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Emerald City of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1910 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/07.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">7</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Patchwork Girl of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1913 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/09.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">8</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Tik-Tok of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1914 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/10.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">9</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Scarecrow of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1915 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/11.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">10</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Rinkitink in Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1916 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/12.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">11</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Lost Princess of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1917 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/13.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">12</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Tin Woodman of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1918 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/14.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">13</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Magic of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1919 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/15.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num\\\">14</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Glinda of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1920 &middot; Full text</span></span></a></li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <h2>Also on this site</h2>\\n    <p class=\\\"section-note HDLmClass80a70a99\\\">Two more Baum works Oz readers love.</p>\\n    <ul class=\\\"grid HDLmClass80a70a99\\\">\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/OzPlay.pdf\\\"><span class=\\\"num extra\\\">PDF</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">The Wizard of Oz: A Dramatic Composition</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1902 &middot; Stage play (PDF)</span></span></a></li>\\n      <li class=\\\"card\\\"><a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/08.htm\\\"><span class=\\\"num extra\\\">Tales</span><span><span class=\\\"title\\\">Little Wizard Stories of Oz</span><span class=\\\"meta\\\">1913 &middot; Six short stories</span></span></a></li>\\n    </ul>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section>\\n    <div class=\\\"signup HDLmClass98e60102\\\">\\n      <h2>Get the free Oz reading guide</h2>\\n      <p>Enter your email and we&rsquo;ll send a one-page reading order, character map and a reminder of where you left off. One short email at a time &mdash; unsubscribe anytime.</p>\\n      <form action=\\\"#\\\" method=\\\"post\\\" novalidate>\\n        <label for=\\\"oz-email\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px;\\\">Email address</label>\\n        <input id=\\\"oz-email\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" placeholder=\\\"you@example.com\\\" required autocomplete=\\\"email\\\">\\n        <button class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Send me the guide</button>\\n      </form>\\n      <p class=\\\"fineprint\\\">We never sell or share your address.</p>\\n    </div>\\n  </section>\\n\\n</main>\\n\\n<footer class=\\\"HDLmClass47d5c5b\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"wrap\\\">\\n    <p>The Marvelous Land of Oz &mdash; a free, ad-light home for L. Frank Baum&rsquo;s complete Oz series. All titles are in the public domain in the United States.</p>\\n    <p><a href=\\\"#books\\\">Browse all books</a> &middot; <a href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start with Book 1</a></p>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"sticky HDLmClass89ba1bed\\\">\\n  <a class=\\\"btn btn-primary\\\" href=\\\"https://themarvelouslandofoz.com/01.htm\\\">Start reading Book 1 &rarr;</a>\\n</div>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added hero title and intro\",\"Why\":\"Orients visitors fast\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass47d5c5b\"},{\"What\":\"Styled links as book cards\",\"Why\":\"Improves scanning and clicks\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass80a70a99\"},{\"What\":\"Added prominent Start reading CTA\",\"Why\":\"Drives clear first action\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass89ba1bed\"},{\"What\":\"Added email signup form\",\"Why\":\"Captures leads for return visits\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass98e60102\"},{\"What\":\"Added responsive mobile styles\",\"Why\":\"Better usability on phones\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass1cb38727\"},{\"What\":\"Fixed Wixard typo\",\"Why\":\"Typos hurt trust\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClass6564b1f4\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm working through computing DJB2 hashes for each proposed improvement, drafting short \"What\" and \"Why\" descriptions for changes like adding a hero section, then running them through the hash algorithm manually.\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nDoing this hash computation by hand for hundreds of characters is too error-prone, so I'm reconsidering scope. I'll trim the improvement strings down to short, punchy What/Why pairs to reduce the arithmetic burden while still keeping the descriptions meaningful, then work through the multiply-add steps carefully.\n\nCounting characters for each improvement's \"what\" and \"why\" text is getting tedious, and I'm reconsidering scaling down to maybe 4 improvements with shorter descriptions to keep the hash computation manageable.\n\nWorking through more improvements: styling links as book cards for easier scanning, adding a prominent \"Start reading\" call-to-action for clear next steps, and including an email signup form, each with character counts to keep within length limits.\n\nI'm reconsidering whether 5 improvements is worth the risk versus fewer, but decide to push forward carefully. I briefly consider a formula-based approach using powers of 33 mod 2^32 but it's not simpler, so I settle on grinding through the hash computation using a 16-bit split method for the multiplication and carry steps.\n\nNow I'm mapping out ASCII codes for letters and computing the hash character by character for the first improvement string.\n\nStill computing the hash...\n\nContinuing the modular multiplication for characters e, r, o, working through each carry and remainder step to build up the hash values.\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation...\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation for characters 19-21 (n, d, space), tracking carry values and remainders through each multiplication step.\n\nContinuing the hash computation through characters t, r, o, O - tracking carry and remainder values at each step as I process the string.\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic decode, processing characters \"e\", \"n\", \"t\" through the same carry-and-divide steps.\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation...\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation for characters \"r\", \"s\", and moving into the next character.\n\nContinuing checksum computation... 47) c=t: computing carry values, arriving at a=1149, b=23643. Now combining these into the final hash value and converting to hex.\n\nThe result is 0x047D5C5B, formatted as \"47d5c5b\" for the hash field, giving \"HDLmClass47d5c5b\". Moving on to the second improvement item about styled book card links, and I'm starting to compute its character codes for the same hashing process.\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nContinuing the digit-by-digit carry propagation for i, n, k...\n\ns, a checksum computation.\n\nContinuing to grind through the modular arithmetic for characters 18-20, tracking carries and remainders through each multiplication step.\n\nContinuing the arithmetic computation, processing characters \"a\", \"r\", \"d\" through the same carry-multiply-diff steps to build up the running hash values.\n\nContinuing the checksum computation through characters 28-30 (m, p, r), tracking carry values and remainders at each step.\n\nContinuing the base-65536 digit extraction for characters 34 through 36, carrying values forward through each multiplication step.\n\nContinuing the multiplication and carry propagation through more characters of the hash computation.\n\nContinuing the arithmetic through characters 45-48, tracking carry values a and b at each step of processing the checksum computation.\n\nContinuing the digit-by-digit modular arithmetic for characters \"ick\", carrying through each multiply-add-divide step.\n\nI get h in hex as 0x80a70a99. Now I'm computing the character-by-character byte sum for \"Added prominent Start reading CTA\" to verify the checksum for improvement 3.\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nStill computing hash values...\n\nContinuing the digit-by-digit base conversion for characters 18 through 20 (t, a, r), tracking carries and remainders through each multiplication step.\n\nContinuing the base-conversion arithmetic for characters 23-25 (r, e, a), tracking carries and remainders through each multiplication step.\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation...\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic decoding, processing characters 35-37 (r, i, v) through the carry calculations.\n\nContinuing the carry-propagation arithmetic for characters 39 through 42, tracking a and b values through each modular multiplication step.\n\nContinuing the base-conversion computation, processing characters 46 and 47 (space and 'f') through the same multiply-carry-subtract steps to update the running values a and b.\n\nContinuing the arithmetic chain, computing carries and remainders for characters \"t\", \" \", and \"a\" step by step through the modular multiplication process.\n\nContinuing the carry-propagation computation through steps 57-58, I get final values a=35258 and b=7149, then I start converting the combined hash value into hexadecimal by breaking 35258 into its hex digits.\n\nFinishing the hex conversion for the second half gives me the string \"89ba1bed\" for that portion. Now I'm setting up the next comparison example, \"Added email signup form\" vs \"Captures leads for return visits,\" matching the common \"Added \" prefix to update the running hash state, then working through the remaining characters one by one.\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation for characters i, l, and space, updating carry and accumulator values at each step.\n\nContinuing the digit-by-digit big-number arithmetic...\n\nContinuing the checksum computation...\n\nContinuing the digit-by-digit big-number division, processing characters t, u, r and updating the carry and remainder values at each step.\n\nContinuing the modular arithmetic computation for characters 32-34, tracking carries and updating a/b values at each step.\n\nContinuing the checksum computation, processing characters 38-40, tracking carries and updating the running a/b values through each step.\n\nContinuing the big-integer multiply-and-encode loop, processing characters 'r', 'e', 't' and updating the running carry/accumulator values step by step.\n\nContinuing the base-conversion arithmetic through characters 32 ('v'), and 118, tracking carries and remainders step by step to decode more of the sequence.\n\